**How to implement.** The unknowns table fixes and frees a parameter, and sets its bounds and prior, through the Items panel's parameter editor, so one editor serves an item's parameter and an opened material's component (001 §O 'the unknowns table (owner, scope, fix / free, bounds, priors, links)'; 001 §O 'Items panel: … a parameter grid (state, value, bounds, σ, provenance)'; AGENTS.md 'Reuse, never copy'). The draft is keyed by the study's parameter reference (`StudyParameterRef`, step 358) in place of an item id and a name, and the editor's view becomes a function both surfaces call; a new function rather than a flag on the old one (the S11.5 brief's study view). Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S11.5. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs`: `ParameterEditDraft` (step 240) holds `parameter : StudyParameterRef` in place of `itemId : ItemId` and `name : ParameterName`; `ofParameter` takes `(parameter : StudyParameterRef) (current : Parameter)`, and `tryState` names `this.parameter.name` where it named the name; every other field and rule is unchanged. `EditItemParameter name` opens `ParameterEditDraft.ofParameter (ItemParameterRef (<the selected item's id>, name))` of the selected item's parameter, as before. `TableAndElementRotationMsg` gains `EditStudyParameter of StudyParameterRef`, documented in one line: a press of a parameter row of the study's unknowns table; its arm opens the draft of an `ItemParameterRef (id, name)` of `kitItems` or of a `MaterialParameterRef (version, name)` of the chosen study's opened material of that version (`model.selectedStudyOpt`, step 410), and changes nothing when neither holds it. It writes nothing, so it is behind no guard. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/ItemsPanelView.fs` (step 241): the editor block becomes `parameterEditorView (model : TableAndElementRotationModel) (draft : ParameterEditDraft) (setWith : ParameterState -> TableAndElementRotationMsg) (dispatch : TableAndElementRotationMsg -> unit) : IView`, public and documented in one to three lines: the block moved whole, its ids, texts, colours and rules unchanged, its `Set` sending `setWith state`. The Items panel shows it when `parameterEditOpt` holds an `ItemParameterRef` of the selected item, with `setWith` `fun state -> SetParameterState (item.id, name, state)` (step 240), so the panel's behaviour is unchanged. The study's unknowns table calls it (step 414). No other view changes. Tests. `ItemsPanelModelTests` (step 240): `the parameter editor starts from the parameter's state and reads the state it sets` keeps its assertions over the draft's `parameter`, `ItemParameterRef (CPL1's id, c2.retardance)`, where it read the item id and the name. `StudyWindowModelTests` (step 410) gains `the study's parameter editor opens on an item parameter or an opened material component, and a parameter it lacks opens nothing`: `EditStudyParameter (ItemParameterRef (CPL1's id, c2.retardance))` opens a draft of `UnknownStateChoice` starting at 1.5 within [1, 2]; with an absorbing crystal material opened by `QZ-LR` (`StudyCommand (OpenMaterial …)` over a user material saved through the window's `materials`, as `StudyMessageTests` saves its own, step 366), `EditStudyParameter (MaterialParameterRef (<its version>, n1))` opens a draft of `KnownStateChoice` at the material's `n1`; and a reference to a parameter neither holds leaves `parameterEditOpt` `None`. `ItemsPanelTests`' `the parameter editor offers Known and Unknown, and Set and Cancel on one row` (step 241) runs as written over the moved block.

**Acceptance.** After the editor is shared, `ParameterEditDraft` MUST be keyed by a `StudyParameterRef`, `EditStudyParameter` MUST open it on an item parameter or an opened material component, and `ItemsPanelView.parameterEditorView` MUST be the one editor view, the Items panel unchanged; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `the study's parameter editor opens on an item parameter or an opened material component, and a parameter it lacks opens nothing`, the count rising by 1, and the changed `the parameter editor starts from the parameter's state and reads the state it sets`; ui-smoke MUST pass; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, their count unchanged; and build, elevation and the twenty s40 invariants MUST pass.
